WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.712
- Every radio definitely
has its own personality.

00:00:04.712 --> 00:00:06.261
This is the boom box your grandmother

00:00:06.261 --> 00:00:09.432
or maybe your great-grandmother
would have carried around.

00:00:09.432 --> 00:00:11.491
This reminds me of a football, actually.

00:00:11.491 --> 00:00:13.792
If you live in a split-level house,

00:00:13.792 --> 00:00:15.959
this is the radio for you.

00:00:20.301 --> 00:00:22.251
This radio has never been opened before,

00:00:22.251 --> 00:00:23.851
'cause this one's a breeze.

00:00:23.851 --> 00:00:25.739
There's not a whole lot of documentation

00:00:25.739 --> 00:00:28.837
that's still around on how to do this.

00:00:28.837 --> 00:00:31.318
Its going too red for my liking.

00:00:31.318 --> 00:00:33.508
You get them in wrong, the radio blows up.

00:00:33.508 --> 00:00:34.857
Sometimes, I work on these radios

00:00:34.857 --> 00:00:36.766
for hours and hours and hours,

00:00:36.766 --> 00:00:38.847
and just when I think
I'm about to give up,

00:00:38.847 --> 00:00:42.264
something clicks in my mind and it works.

00:00:48.038 --> 00:00:51.708
To me, this radio looks
very science fiction like.

00:00:51.708 --> 00:00:55.625
This would be like the
console of a space ship.

00:00:58.577 --> 00:01:00.788
It started off as a
hobby and now its become

00:01:00.788 --> 00:01:03.121
a little bit more than that.

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:08.670
I have several hundred at any given point.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.502
These radios are found
in dumps and garages

00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:12.835
and old closets.

00:01:13.811 --> 00:01:16.102
There were families that
probably sat around these radios

00:01:16.102 --> 00:01:19.830
and listened to the first
man land on the moon.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.960
FDR's Fireside Chats were probably playing

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.710
through these radios.

00:01:26.291 --> 00:01:29.131
Digital technology sterilizes music.

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:31.742
Old radios sound a lot more organic,

00:01:31.742 --> 00:01:32.825
a lot warmer.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.451
When I repair these radios I feel like

00:01:36.451 --> 00:01:39.534
I'm giving them back their old voice.

